Carried from pingdotgg/t3code PR #25930, "feat(scheduled-tasks): optionally run a missed fixed-time slot once when
back" (https://github.com/pingdotgg/t3code/pull/25930), head 174f1eafa3, diffed against its merge base with main
(2fbb071e0c). Applies to v0.1.12 as is (line offsets only).

What it does: a fixed-time schedule takes `missedRun: "skip" | "run_once"`. With "run_once", a time missed while T3
was off or asleep (normally skipped once it is more than 10 minutes late) runs once when T3 is back; several missed
times coalesce into one run. Omitted on save keeps the stored value. The server advertises `missedRunSchedules`; the
web editor shows a "Run once if missed" switch for "At a time" tasks; schedule_task (MCP) takes it through the shared
schema.

Changed from upstream: trimmed to what ships in this build; no behaviour change. Left out:
- apps/mobile/** (the mobile app isn't part of this package),
- the 20 web/mobile translation catalogs (an untranslated string falls back to its English source, and English never
  reads a catalog),
- docs/user/project-settings.md,
- the tests (Schedule, ScheduledTaskService.schedule, ServerEnvironment, web logic; they run in upstream's CI) and
  apps/server/src/provider/agentContextBudget.json, which only the context-budget test reads: in this tree that test
  is 236 bytes over budget (the schedule_task trigger description grew).
Reviewed against 0.1.12 (Schedule.isMissedFixedTimeRun, ScheduledTaskService.runDueTasks/upsert, the web draft):
nothing to fix.

Replace with upstream: as soon as a T3 release includes #25930. Our tasks set `missedRun` explicitly
(nexus-sessions plugin/hooks/schedules.js), so upstream's field name and values are what has to match.

